# The settings list's other ending: every way of leaving it that throws the change away. A row's
# editor cancelled, the list cancelled with an accepted row inside it, and the list reopened to show
# that nothing was written.
#
#   python tools/walkthrough/walk.py tools/walkthrough/settings-cancel.walk

# The panel's design, which the composition sets once on a device: a leaf that names no family draws
# in it, and the band's height picks the cut.
set-font ttyp0

# Up held to a double opens the list on the unit row.
load home
send up:double
wait 1 s

# Down to the jingle, Forward into its choices, and Down twice to the third entry. Cancel hands the
# list the key it opened on rather than the one showing, so JINGLE reads Poacher again.
send down:single
wait 1 s
send forward:single
wait 1 s
send down:single
wait 1 s
send down:single
wait 1 s
send cancel:single
wait 1 s

# The same in the unit's choices, stepped two entries to inHg and cancelled: the row still reads
# kPa.
send up:single
wait 1 s
send forward:single
wait 1 s
send down:single
wait 1 s
send down:single
wait 1 s
send cancel:single
wait 1 s

# The duration editor opened, nudged a minute and cancelled: the row still reads fifteen minutes.
send down:single
wait 1 s
send down:single
wait 1 s
send forward:single
wait 1 s
send up:single
wait 1 s
send cancel:single
wait 1 s

# The same editor again, nudged and accepted: the row now holds sixteen minutes, which is a change
# the list has taken but not yet written.
send forward:single
wait 1 s
send up:single
wait 1 s
send ok:single
wait 1 s

# Cancel on the rows is the list's own: the set goes back to the one it opened on and the page pops
# without the device writing anything.
send cancel:single
wait 1 s

# Opened again, the list reads fifteen minutes: the accepted change died with the list that held it.
send up:double
wait 1 s

# Cancel once more leaves the home page as it was found, with no save behind either visit.
send cancel:single
wait 1 s

emit
